From 49237f17a9ea6460ce56c01d844317ad17a9347a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:43:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Non linear solvers: iterations of the linear solver in the
 messages

The number of iterations of an iterative linear solver is recorded for each
iteration of the `Newton` and `FixedPoint` solvers (information on the
iterations, `LinearSolver/NumberOfIterations`), but was not written: in the
messages of a computation, the number of iterations of the linear solver
could not be separated from their cost, which a study of scalability needs
at each size.

When the iterations are printed, a line follows each linear solve of an
iterative solver:

    Fixed point iteration  3 : 17 iterations of the linear solver
    Newton iteration  3 : 17 iterations of the linear solver

Nothing is written for a direct solver, nor when the iterations are not
printed. The lines giving the norm of the residual are unchanged.

The prediction, which writes no message, and the `KINSOL` and `SNES`
solvers, which do not record these iterations, are unchanged.

FixedPointSolverTest: in all its computations (Newton and fixed point
solvers, direct and iterative linear solvers, with and without line
search), the numbers of iterations written in the messages of each time
step are the ones recorded, in the same order.
